sxml xquery - Run an XQuery 4.0 query

Usage: sxml xquery [--context-item=FILE] [--expression=TEXT] [--param=NAME=VALUE]... [--method=METHOD] [--locations=WHEN] [--allow-file-access] [--collection=DIR] [--allow-put] [--code-language=LIBRARY]... [--output=FILE] [--force] [QUERY-FILE]

Runs the XQuery 4.0 main module in QUERY-FILE, or the query that
--expression gives, and writes the result to standard output. The
result is serialized as the query's output declarations say (method
xml unless they name another); --method replaces the method.

--context-item=FILE parses FILE and makes it the context item.
--param=NAME=VALUE binds the external variable $NAME, if the query
declares it, to xs:untypedAtomic(VALUE). Library modules (import
module ... at) are read from local files relative to the working
directory; fn:doc reads local files. --allow-file-access lets the
query read and write files with the EXPath File functions
(namespace http://expath.org/ns/file); without it they do not exist.

An updating query (the XQuery Update Facility 3.0) writes the
context item's document as its updates left it; FILE itself is
not changed. fn:put stores documents only with --allow-put, which
writes each to the local file its URI names (relative URIs are in
the working directory); without it fn:put raises FOUP0002.

--output=FILE (-o FILE) writes the result to FILE instead. Files are
written only when the query succeeds; one that exists is replaced
only with --force.

--locations=WHEN: whether the documents read keep the line and column
of each node, for fn:location: automatic (the default) when the query
calls fn:location, can look up functions or imports a schema,
always, or never.

An error is reported on standard error as
  QUERY-FILE:LINE:COLUMN: err:CODE: description
and, when its value is a node whose document kept its locations,
  FILE:LINE:COLUMN: the node the error names

Exit status: 0 on success, 1 for an error in the query or a context
document that is not well-formed, 3 when a file cannot be read or
written.

Options:
  -h, --help                   Show this help and exit
      --context-item=FILE      XML document to use as the context item; - reads standard input
      --expression=TEXT        The query itself, instead of QUERY-FILE
      --param=NAME=VALUE       Bind external variable $NAME to xs:untypedAtomic(VALUE) (repeatable)
      --method=METHOD          Serialization method of the result, replacing the query's (one of: adaptive, xml, xhtml, html, text, json, csv)
      --locations=WHEN         Keep the line and column of input nodes, for fn:location (one of: automatic, always, never; default: automatic)
      --allow-file-access      Let the query read and write files (EXPath File functions)
      --collection=DIR         Directory whose XML files are the default collection
      --allow-put              Let fn:put write the documents it stores to local files
      --code-language=LIBRARY  Load a tree-sitter language for tree-sitter:parse from a shared library (repeatable)
  -o, --output=FILE            Write the result to FILE instead of standard output
      --force                  Replace files that exist instead of refusing

Arguments:
  QUERY-FILE  File holding the XQuery 4.0 main module; - reads standard input

Examples:
  sxml xquery --context-item=draft.xml requirements.xq
  sxml xquery --expression='for $i in 1 to 3 return <i>{$i}</i>'
  sxml xquery --param=n=5 --expression='declare variable $n external; $n * 2'
  sxml xquery --allow-put --context-item=draft.xml --expression='put(., "copy.xml")'
